# PBE0 on helium -- the smallest deck on a HYBRID functional.
#
# Every other `scf` deck here is either pure Hartree-Fock (`xc hf`) or pure DFT
# (`xc lda`), so nothing exercised the path where exact exchange and a
# semilocal functional are combined. That path had two defects:
#
#   * the exact-exchange energy was accumulated into `exc` and then overwritten
#     by the DFT contribution, so it never reached the total energy. The
#     orbitals were right and only the reported number was wrong, which is
#     exactly the kind of error a deck catches and inspection does not.
#
#   * a hybrid named by its libxc name rather than by one of the aliases got no
#     exact exchange at all, because the admixture was hardcoded per alias
#     instead of queried from libxc.
#
# `pbe0` is the alias form; `HYB_GGA_XC_PBEH` is the same functional by its
# libxc name and must give the same energy. The equality of the two admixtures
# is checked directly in `test_dft`.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc scf_he_pbe0.in)

dft
    xc       pbe0
    maxiter  10
    econv    1e-4
    dconv    1e-3
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    He  0.0  0.0  0.0
end
